Ambient `declare function`, `class`, `interface`, and `type` declarations keep their type parameters (`<T>`, `<K, V>`) in their outline lines; the type alias prints without its `= …` value.
== args
input/ambient.d.ts
== file input/ambient.d.ts
declare function parse<T>(text: string): T;
declare class Store<K, V> {}
declare interface Lookup<K> {}
declare type Maybe<T> = T | null;
== stdout
input/ambient.d.ts (4 lines)
[L1-L1] declare function parse<T>(text: string): T
[L2-L2] declare class Store<K, V>
[L3-L3] declare interface Lookup<K>
[L4-L4] declare type Maybe<T>
== stderr
== exit 0
